<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="6357a7a1">&lt;p&gt;
    The rollback plan presents the specifications, criteria, procedures, and responsibilities to follow to revert
    a release or system into a previous state or defined interim state.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Compile the rollback plan to include activities and tasks to be followed in various trigger scenarios, to revert a
    deployed application or business capability to the last-known-good configuration or to a manual backup process,
    including operations activities, interim procedures and customer, stakeholder and employee communications.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Scenario 1, a “no-go” decision is made immediately prior to conversion to a new system or release:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify key stakeholders to provide a justification to invoke the rollback and seek approval for taking action
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify vendors and internal support personnel to stop scheduled installation
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify business and conversion support personnel to cancel migration to new policies and procedures and schedule
        changes
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify customers of service disruption and schedule changes
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify employee and customer communication representatives&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Scenario 2, a “no-go” decision is made after a conversion has started:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        De-install new application
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Revert to the previous state – the system scheduled for decommissioning
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reinstate original procedures, forms, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify personnel to move to off-line procedures in certain situations (e.g., the re-install is not completed by a
        certain time)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify personnel of schedule changes
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Distribute customer communications
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify personnel to shift focus to contingency procedures
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    To determine that the process is viable and feasible, test the fail-over process prior to the deployment event.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
